  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As soon as I start the game, in my home, I'm stuck in the AFK state, as if my headset went to sleep or I opened the SteamVR overlay. Going to sleep and returning, as well as opening and closing the Steam overlay does not let me leave AFK state. Same with restarting the game, toggling sitting/standing, or changing locomotion styles. I'm able to go to different worlds and access the new menus (looking great btw), but I can't interact with anything in the world like the camera.\n(I'm in my AFK animation, I cannot see my avatar's head and the AFK icon appears in the bottom right, I'm pretty sure this is regular AFK behavior.)\nI'm on a full stock Valve Index, Lighthouses 2.0 and Knuckles Controllers. I don't have any custom binds. This is my first time trying the beta however.\n\nUPDATE: I was able to at least disable it by turning off \"AFK Detection\" from the radial config menu. It AFK's me as soon as I turn it back on again.",
